ate to be the one to tell you this but  that guy your neighbour Jerry he's a  vampire originally mintz-plasse wasn't  feeling a reboot but he couldn't pass up  the chance to work with Collin Farrel  mintz-plasse told HitFix I'm not the  biggest fan of mice cuz you know I sit  and watch the trailers oh my gosh think  of a new freaking idea you know but he  was on board once he saw the cast list  and I saw the Anton and Colin and gray  and Craig were all attached if done  right it could be this really memorable  role for the movie almost a sitcom star  in 2012 mintz-plasse was on track to  have his own TV series friend me written  by writer Alan Kirschenbaum  unfortunately friend me was cancelled  after Kherson mom passed away  mintz-plasse tweeted r.i.p alan only  worked with you for 10 days but thanks  so much for this wonderful job you were  a funny great guy but mintz-plasse  landed on TV for real when he booked  2016's the Great Indoors  it is so incredible to meet you on Clark  online content curator hi Clark  obviously made-up job title while the  show was cancelled after just one season  mintz-plasse his performance proved he  could be sitcom gold in the right part  musically inclined mintz-plasse has  appeared in a slew of music videos  perhaps most notably he played drums in  Kid Cudi's late 60s inspired erase me  mintz-plasse also appeared alongside  kick-ass co-star Chloe grace Moretz for  the soft packs answer to yourself as  well as unknown Mortal orchestras so  good at being in trouble most recently  he starred as a kidnapper in Alice in  Wonderland's you don't know and a man  who overcomes life in a wheelchair in  coda lines ready  rocking out mintz-plasse isn't just  music video I can he's also in a band  after playing drums for young rasp  scallions for eight years before they  broke up  mintz-plasse and his friend Adam a  seraph say they started getting high  jamming out in the backyard and calling  themselves bear on fire when they  realized that things were getting groovy  the duo recruited some friends and  released their first studio album in  2015  though shottsford McLovin inevitably  followed the actor wherever he plays  mintz-plasse doesn't mind he told  Stereogum I just want as many people to  come to the show and as many people to  hear my music as possible going dark  when it comes to future work  mintz-plasse is most interested in  darker more dramatic roles however going  dark in the kick-ass series wasn't the  easiest thing for the actor he told the  Belfast Telegraph I read the script and  I was nervous because it's unlike  anything I've ever done before  so I got an acting coach a month before  filming we would go through every scene  in every line and figure out where the  character needed to go emotionally  mintz-plasse also studied some other  villainous characters from the big  screen to help him get it right and some  from real life too he said I watched  Heath Ledger's Joker quite a bit and I  researched Marvel's The Punisher I also  watched this really dark serial killer  on trial I studied his eyes and how  lifeless they were and tried to use that  too a far cry from McLovin innocent baby  face but these days he truly wants to  kick some ass thanks for watching click  the looper icon to subscribe to our  YouTube channel let's check out all this  cool stuff we know you love to  you

